        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-01T03:22:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a little incongruous to me, and I\u0027m having some trouble getting my head around it.\nConditionally compiling HDMI support for an optional sub-board type may be\nbetter handled by having a separate nissa/src/hdmi.c, and remove HDMI references\nfrom this file, and having a separate HOOK_INIT in the other file for HDMI init.",
      "revId": "70ccd850dea3b0b3361eaaae37779d4ce42ca459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bcfea4b_233e99af",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/nissa/src/sub_board.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-01T22:52:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there\u0027s value in keeping all the sub-board configuration in the same place, since they all operate on the same few resources so it\u0027s easier to reason about what it\u0027s doing.\n\nThis is conditionally compiled because some boards don\u0027t define the GPIO aliases, so what if we added a `GPIO_DT_FROM_ALIAS_OR` macro that allows it to still be built but early-return if used for some reason?",
      "parentUuid": "e36f46a7_6a6a01bd",
      "revId": "70ccd850dea3b0b3361eaaae37779d4ce42ca459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad7f35df_1a0287f2",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/nissa/src/sub_board.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T00:34:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a tradeoff, and at some point it might make sense to split the HDMI handling out if more boards are not supporting it. Happy to leave it in the same file for now, if that\u0027s what you think is best.\n\nSo I am not sure why some boards haven\u0027t added the aliases. The easiest fix is\nmaybe just add the aliases so it is consistent (the DTS contract here is that\nany of these gpios should go through an alias).\nIf it\u0027s the situation that these boards don\u0027t use HDMI, then maybe that code should be conditionally compiled using the NISSA_BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT guard.",
      "parentUuid": "1bcfea4b_233e99af",
      "revId": "70ccd850dea3b0b3361eaaae37779d4ce42ca459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71bab4aa_18362103",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/nissa/src/sub_board.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T00:58:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Xivu doesn\u0027t support HDMI at all, so it doesn\u0027t define those IOs. It would be wrong to add them. The `BOARD_HAS_HDMI_SUPPORT` guard is currently set based on whether the aliases exist, so I think that does what you\u0027re thinking.\n\nI prefer to leave it like this for now, but we might revisit later.",
      "parentUuid": "ad7f35df_1a0287f2",
      "revId": "70ccd850dea3b0b3361eaaae37779d4ce42ca459",
